                <pb facs="0406" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg312"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/3124: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Jose</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-04-26T09:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                                1924—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:47 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>25. Department’s April 23, 1 p.m. received evening April 24th badly garbled.
                    Please repeat by cable direct.</p>
                <p>President Acosta in favor of participation of Costa Rica in the Amapala
                    conference. On account of political conditions due to uncertainty in connection
                    with change of administration May 1st the President is apparently encountering
                    some difficulty in a representative. He hopes however to announce nomination
                    soon. Repeated to Central American missions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
